  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 1411.01 Operator Duties",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 1411.01 Operator Duties. Each operator shall:\n\n(a) Except as otherwise required by Saf-C 1402.01(c), construct, install, maintain, and operate each challenge course or zip line in accordance with the standards set forth in either the “ANSI/ACCT 03-2019 CHALLENGE COURSES AND CANOPY/ZIP LINE TOURS STANDARDS” (Revision of ANSI/ACCT 03-2016 Standards) or the ASTM International standards listed in Saf-C 1402.01(a), available as noted in Appendix B;\n\n(b) Ensure that each challenge course or zip line is inspected, at least once each year, by a qualified person, as defined in either the “ANSI/ACCT 03-2019 CHALLENGE COURSES AND CANOPY/ZIP LINE TOURS STANDARDS” (Revision of ANSI/ACCT 03-2016 Standards) or the ASTM International standards listed in Saf-C 1402.01(a), available as noted in Appendix B, and found to be in safe condition;\n\n(c) Train employees for each challenge course or zip line in accordance with either the “ANSI/ACCT 03-2019 CHALLENGE COURSES AND CANOPY/ZIP LINE TOURS STANDARDS” (Revision of ANSI/ACCT 03-2016 Standards) or the ASTM International standards listed in Saf-C 1402.01(a), available as noted in Appendix B;\n\n(d) Procure and maintain insurance pursuant to RSA 321-A:5 and Saf-C 1405.06;\n\n(e) Retain all records pertaining to inspections and maintenance for a period of 2 years in accordance with RSA 321-A:2-a, I(a)(4); and\n\n(f) Comply with the accident procedures set forth in Saf-C 1405.04.\n\nSource. #12615, eff 8-28-18; ss by #13666, eff 6-20-23; ss by #14139, eff 11-28-24, EXPIRES: 11-28-34 (see Revision Note #3 at chapter heading for Saf-C 1400)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c1400.html"
}
